:R-HSA-2022870  a           obo:GO_0050650 , owl:NamedIndividual ;
        rdfs:comment        "Chondroitin sulfate (CS) glycosaminoglycan consists of N-acetylgalactosamine (GalNAc) residues alternating in glycosidic linkages with glucuronic acid (GlcA). GalNAc residues are sulfated to varying degrees on 4- and/or 6- positions. The steps below describe the biosynthesis of a simple CS molecule (Pavao et al. 2006, Silbert & Sugumaran 2002)." , "Automated change 2025-02-13: GO:0030206 replaced by GO:0050650" ;
